  "before_interfaces": {
    "def-tgr-stationary-thermal-carriers": [
      null,
      "## Definition\n\nLet $(M,g,N_0)$ be a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold of signature\n$(-,+,+,+)$ in the sense of [[def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects]], and let\n$\\nabla$ be its unique torsion-free $g$-compatible connection supplied by\n[[thm-gr-nondegenerate-levi-civita-and-tensor-derivative]]. Fix a nonempty\nconnected open set $O\\subseteq M$. A **selected stationary thermal carrier** on\n$O$ consists of a smooth future timelike vector field $\\xi$ and a smooth\npositive scalar field $T:O\\to(0,\\infty)$, where $T$ is measured in kelvins,\nsuch that $\\xi$ is a Killing field of $g$ in the sense of\n[[def-gr-killing-field]]. Equivalently, the criterion is\n$\\nabla_{(a}\\xi_{b)}=0$ by\n[[thm-gr-killing-and-on-shell-matter-identities]]. The round brackets mean\nsymmetrization with factor $1/2$. The choice of $\\xi$ specifies the thermal congruence; no\ncoordinate chart or universal observer field is selected.\n\nSet $N_\\xi:=\\sqrt{-g(\\xi,\\xi)}>0$ and $u:=\\xi/N_\\xi$. Then\n$g(u,u)=-1$. In the length-coordinate convention $x^0=ct$, $u$ is\ndimensionless and $cu$ is the physical four-velocity, with $c>0$ in\n$\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$. For a fixed Boltzmann constant $k_B>0$ in\n$\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, define the inverse-temperature vector\n$\\beta:=u/(k_BT)$, with units $\\mathrm{J^{-1}}$, and the Killing-normalized\ntemperature field $T_K:=N_\\xi T$. Thus $\\beta=\\xi/(k_BT_K)$; this definition\ndoes not assert that $T_K$ is constant.\n\nFor a smooth chemical-potential scalar $\\mu:O\\to\\mathbb R$ in joules, put\n$\\zeta:=\\mu/(k_BT)$, a dimensionless scalar. Define the rest-space metric,\nderivative, acceleration, expansion and shear by\n$$h_{ab}:=g_{ab}+u_au_b,\\qquad D:=u^a\\nabla_a,\\qquad a_b:=u^a\\nabla_au_b,\\qquad \\theta:=\\nabla_au^a,\\qquad \\sigma_{ab}:=h_a{}^ch_b{}^d\\nabla_{(c}u_{d)}-\\frac13\\theta h_{ab}.$$\nHere $a$, $\\theta$ and $\\sigma$ have inverse-length units; the physical\nproper acceleration is $c^2a$. The smooth tangent-bundle structure used by\nthe cited GR suppliers assumes the Axiom of Countable Choice\n[[def-countable-choice]]; no stronger choice principle is part of this\ndefinition."
    ],
    "def-tgr-future-mass-shell-measure": [
      null,
      "## Definition\n\nLet $(M,g,N_0)$ be a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold of signature\n$(-,+,+,+)$ [[def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects]], let $x\\in M$, and let\n$M_*>0$ be a rest-energy parameter in joules. The **future massive shell at\n$x$** is the Borel subset\n$$\\mathcal H^+_{M_*,x}:=\\{P\\in T_xM:g_x(P,P)=-M_*^2,\\ P\\text{ future-directed}\\}.$$\nUse any smooth future orthonormal tetrad near $x$, whose existence is\n[[thm-gr-local-lorentz-tetrad-existence]]. At $x$ write its basis as\n$(e_0,e_1,e_2,e_3)$ and, for $q=(q_1,q_2,q_3)\\in\\mathbb R^3$ with energy\ncoordinates in joules, put\n$$E(q):=\\sqrt{M_*^2+|q|^2},\\qquad P_e(q):=E(q)e_0+\\sum_{i=1}^3q_i e_i.$$\nLet $\\lambda_3$ be Euclidean Lebesgue measure on $\\mathbb R^3$\n([[def-lebesgue-measure-and-the-lebesgue-sigma-algebra]],\n[[thm-lebesgue-measure-is-a-complete-measure]]). For every Borel set\n$A\\subseteq\\mathcal H^+_{M_*,x}$, with its subspace Borel sigma-algebra\n([[def-borel-sigma-algebra]]), define\n$$\\mu_{M_*,x,e}(A):=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}\\mathbf1_A(P_e(q))\\,\\frac{1}{E(q)}\\,d\\lambda_3(q).$$\nIn these tetrad coordinates the shell equation is\n$-(P^0)^2+|q|^2=-M_*^2$, and the future sheet has $P^0>0$, hence\n$P^0=E(q)$. Thus $P_e$ is a bijection onto the shell with continuous inverse\n$q_i=g(P,e_i)$, so it is a homeomorphism. Continuous preimages of Borel sets are Borel\n([[thm-continuous-preimages-of-borel-sets-are-borel]]), and\n$1/E(q)$ is a positive continuous density. The nonnegative Lebesgue integral\nover a measurable set is [[def-integral-over-a-measurable-set]]; the\npositive-density measure theorem [[thm-indefinite-integral-of-a-nonnegative-function-is-a-measure]] makes\n$\\mu_{M_*,x,e}$ a positive Borel measure. Its coordinate expression is\n$d^3q/E(q)$ and its units are $\\mathrm{J^2}$.\n\nTheorem [[lem-tgr-mass-shell-measure-tetrad-invariance]] proves that this\nmeasure is independent of the chosen future orthonormal tetrad. We therefore\nwrite it as $\\mu_{M_*,x}$, or $d\\mu_{M_*}$ when the fiber is understood. The\nunderlying Lebesgue and tetrad suppliers use $\\mathrm{AC}_\\omega$ exactly as\ndeclared by [[def-countable-choice]]; no arbitrary-index choice is asserted."
    ],
    "lem-tgr-killing-thermal-normalization": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nLet $O$ and the smooth fields $(g,\\nabla,\\xi,T,u,N_\\xi,\\beta)$ be as in\n[[def-tgr-stationary-thermal-carriers]]. Then\n$$\\beta\\text{ is Killing}\\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad N_\\xi T=T_K\\text{ for a constant }T_K>0.$$\nWhen this holds, $\\beta=\\xi/(k_BT_K)$, and the Killing congruence has\n$$\\xi(N_\\xi)=0,\\qquad a=\\nabla\\log N_\\xi,\\qquad \\theta=0,\\qquad \\sigma_{ab}=0.$$\nIf $\\xi$ is replaced by $b\\xi$ with a constant $b>0$, then\n$N_\\xi$ and $T_K$ scale by $b$, while $u$ and $\\beta$ are unchanged."
    ],
    "lem-tgr-thermal-killing-kinematic-equivalence": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nLet $O$ be a connected open set in a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian\nfour-manifold, let $u$ be a smooth future unit timelike vector field on $O$\n($g(u,u)=-1$), and let $T:O\\to(0,\\infty)$ be smooth. Define\n$\\beta:=u/(k_BT)$, $h_{ab}:=g_{ab}+u_au_b$,\n$D:=u^a\\nabla_a$, $a_b:=u^a\\nabla_au_b$,\n$\\theta:=\\nabla_au^a$ and\n$\\sigma_{ab}:=h_a{}^ch_b{}^d\\nabla_{(c}u_{d)}-\\theta h_{ab}/3$ as in\n[[def-tgr-stationary-thermal-carriers]]. Then $\\beta$ is a Killing field of\n$g$ (equivalently $\\nabla_{(a}\\beta_{b)}=0$ by\n[[def-gr-killing-field]] and\n[[thm-gr-killing-and-on-shell-matter-identities]]) if and only if\n$$DT=0,\\qquad \\theta=0,\\qquad \\sigma_{ab}=0,\\qquad h_a{}^b\\nabla_b\\log T=-a_a.$$\nNo hypersurface-orthogonality or vanishing-vorticity condition is assumed."
    ],
    "lem-tgr-isometry-natural-tensor-invariance": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nLet $(M,g,N_0)$ be a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold\n[[def-gr-smooth-lorentzian-objects]], let $O\\subseteq M$ be open, and let\n$\\xi$ be a smooth nowhere-zero vector field on $O$ satisfying\n$\\nabla_{(a}\\xi_{b)}=0$ for the unique metric-selected connection $\\nabla$\n[[thm-gr-nondegenerate-levi-civita-and-tensor-derivative]]. Its local flow\n$\\Phi_s$ exists on the open flow\ndomains supplied by [[thm-flow-box-theorem]]. On every common flow domain,\n$\\Phi_s$ is a local isometry and preserves $\\nabla$ and $\\xi$. Consequently\nit preserves the curvature tensor $R$ of\n[[def-gr-curvature-tensor-and-derived-tensors]], all finite covariant\nderivatives of $R$ and $\\xi$, and every tensor or scalar obtained from these\nfields by finitely many tensor products, contractions, and smooth scalar\noperations. The assertion is local; it assumes no complete flow or global\nisometry group. It makes no claim about arbitrary quantum observables or their\nanalytic representation by local curvature data."
    ],
    "lem-tgr-mass-shell-polynomial-rigidity": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nLet $(V,g,C^+)$ be a four-dimensional time-oriented Lorentz vector space of\nsignature $(-,+,+,+)$, with future cone $C^+$ as in\n[[def-time-orientation-and-future-causal-sets]]. Let $M>0$ and let $A$ be a\nsymmetric bilinear form on $V$ and $b$ a covector. If\n$$A(P,P)+b(P)=0\\qquad\\text{for every }P\\in C^+\\text{ with }g(P,P)=-M^2,$$\nthen $A=0$ and $b=0$. If instead this identity holds for every nonzero future\nnull vector $P\\in\\overline{C^+}$, then $b=0$ and $A=\\lambda g$ for some\n$\\lambda\\in\\mathbb R$. The second clause is the exact massless conformal\nexception."
    ],
    "lem-tgr-mass-shell-measure-tetrad-invariance": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nLet $x$ be an event of a time-oriented smooth Lorentzian four-manifold, let\n$M_*>0$, and let $e$ and $e'$ be any two smooth future orthonormal tetrads\nnear $x$. The measures $d\\mu_{M_*,x,e}$ and $d\\mu_{M_*,x,e'}$ defined in\n[[def-tgr-future-mass-shell-measure]] agree on every Borel subset of the future\nmassive shell at $x$. Hence the fiber measure $d\\mu_{M_*,x}$ is independent of\nthe chosen future orthonormal tetrad."
    ],
    "thm-tgr-juttner-partition-and-moments": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nLet $x$ be an event in a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian four-manifold, let\n$M_*>0$ be an energy in joules, and let $u\\in T_xM$ be future unit timelike,\n$g(u,u)=-1$. Fix $k_B>0$ in $\\mathrm{J\\,K^{-1}}$, $T>0$ in kelvins,\n$n>0$ in $\\mathrm{m^{-3}}$, $c>0$ in $\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$, and a reference\naction $h_{\\rm ref}>0$ in $\\mathrm{J\\,s}$. Put\n$$\\alpha:=\\frac1{k_BT},\\qquad \\beta:=\\frac{u}{k_BT},\\qquad E_u(P):=-g(P,u).$$\nFor $j=0,1,2,3$ and $z>0$ define\n$$K_j(z):=\\int_0^\\infty e^{-z\\cosh t}\\cosh(jt)\\,dt.$$\nWith the future-shell measure of [[def-tgr-future-mass-shell-measure]], define\n$$I_{M_*}(\\alpha):=\\int_{\\mathcal H^+_{M_*,x}}e^{g(\\beta,P)}\\,d\\mu_{M_*}(P),\\qquad Z_{M_*}(\\alpha):=\\int_{\\mathbb R^3}e^{-\\alpha E(q)}\\,d^3q,$$\nwhere $E(q)=\\sqrt{M_*^2+|q|^2}$ in a future orthonormal tetrad whose time\naxis is $u$. Both integrals are finite and positive, and\n$$I_{M_*}(\\alpha)=\\frac{4\\pi M_*}{\\alpha}K_1(\\alpha M_*),\\qquad Z_{M_*}(\\alpha)=\\frac{4\\pi M_*^2}{\\alpha}K_2(\\alpha M_*).$$\nThe observer-rest momentum law\n$$d\\nu_u(q):=Z_{M_*}(\\alpha)^{-1}e^{-\\alpha E(q)}d^3q$$\nis a probability measure. Define the dimensionless occupation and its number\ncurrent and stress moments by\n$$\\zeta:=\\log\\!\\left(\\frac{n h_{\\rm ref}^3c^3}{Z_{M_*}(\\alpha)}\\right),\\qquad f(P):=e^{\\zeta+g(\\beta,P)},$$\n$$J^a:=(h_{\\rm ref}^3c^3)^{-1}\\int_{\\mathcal H^+_{M_*,x}}P^a f(P)\\,d\\mu_{M_*}(P),\\qquad T^{ab}:=(h_{\\rm ref}^3c^3)^{-1}\\int_{\\mathcal H^+_{M_*,x}}P^aP^b f(P)\\,d\\mu_{M_*}(P).$$\nThese integrals converge, and, with\n$$\\varepsilon:=n\\left(M_*\\frac{K_1(\\alpha M_*)}{K_2(\\alpha M_*)}+\\frac3\\alpha\\right),\\qquad p:=\\frac n\\alpha=nk_BT,$$\nthey satisfy $J^a=nu^a$ and\n$T^{ab}=(\\varepsilon+p)u^au^b+pg^{ab}$. The quantities $J$ and $T$ have\nunits $\\mathrm{m^{-3}}$ and $\\mathrm{J\\,m^{-3}}$, respectively. The reference\naction $h_{\\rm ref}$ is only a declared phase-space unit convention; it is\nnot Planck's constant or a measured parameter."
    ],
    "thm-tgr-massive-juttner-stationarity": [
      null,
      "## Statement\n\nLet $O$ be a connected open subset of a smooth time-oriented Lorentzian\nfour-manifold with metric-selected connection $\\nabla$. Let $M_*>0$ be a\nrest-energy, let $\\beta$ be a smooth vector field with units\n$\\mathrm{J^{-1}}$, let $\\zeta:O\\to\\mathbb R$ be smooth and dimensionless, and\ndefine on the future massive shell\n$$f(x,P):=\\exp\\bigl(\\zeta(x)+g_x(\\beta(x),P)\\bigr),\\qquad \\mathcal L:=P^a\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x^a}-\\Gamma^a{}_{bc}P^bP^c\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial P^a}.$$\nThe geodesic Liouville vector field $\\mathcal L$ is tangent to\n$\\mathcal H^+_{M_*,x}$ and\n$$\\mathcal Lf=0\\text{ on every future massive shell} \\quad\\Longleftrightarrow\\quad \\nabla_{(a}\\beta_{b)}=0\\text{ and }d\\zeta=0,$$\nwhere $\\nabla_{(a}\\beta_{b)}=0$ is the covariant Killing condition\n([[def-gr-killing-field]], [[thm-gr-killing-and-on-shell-matter-identities]]).\nSince $O$ is connected, $d\\zeta=0$ means $\\zeta$ is constant on $O$.\n\nFor any vector $\\beta_x\\in T_xM$, define its shell normalizer by\n$$I_{M_*}(\\beta_x):=\\int_{\\mathcal H^+_{M_*,x}}e^{g_x(\\beta_x,P)}\\,d\\mu_{M_*,x}(P).$$\nThis integral is finite exactly when $\\beta_x$ is future timelike. If so, with\n$\\alpha:=\\sqrt{-g_x(\\beta_x,\\beta_x)}>0$, it equals\n$4\\pi M_*K_1(\\alpha M_*)/\\alpha$ as in\n[[thm-tgr-juttner-partition-and-moments]]. In particular, for carrier data\n$\\beta=u/(k_BT)$, the choice\n$$\\zeta=\\log\\!\\left(\\frac{n h_{\\rm ref}^3c^3}{Z_{M_*}(1/(k_BT))}\\right)$$\nnormalizes the proper number density to $n$ and gives exactly the number\ncurrent and stress moments of\n[[thm-tgr-juttner-partition-and-moments]]. This is a mathematical theorem about\nthe specified exponential ansatz; it does not assert that a material\nthermalizes or that a physical equilibrium state exists."
    ],
    "ex-tgr-flrw-no-killing-equilibrium": [
      null
    ]
  }
